hadiths[67]{hadithnumber,text}:
"471","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Eid al-Fitr is the day when you break your fast, and Eid al-Adha is the day when you offer sacrifices."""
"472","It is narrated from Salamah bin Akwa’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to perform ghusl (ritual bath) on the day of Eid."
"473","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father, who narrates from his grandfather, that the Prophet ﷺ used to wear a striped Yemeni cloak on every Eid."
"474","It is narrated from Matlib bin Abdullah bin Hantab that on the day of Eid, the Prophet ﷺ would go to the Eid ground in the morning by a large road, and when returning, he would come back by another road near the house of Ammar bin Yasir (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"475","Abdur Rahman Taymi narrates from his father that he saw the Prophet ﷺ returning from the Eid prayer ground on the day of Eid. The Prophet ﷺ passed by the date sellers beneath the market. When he ﷺ reached near Masjid al-A'raj, which was by the unpaved pond in the market, he ﷺ stood with his feet apart, facing the qiblah, near the tribe of Salm. He ﷺ made supplication and then returned."
"476","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when he would go out towards the Eid ground on the day of Eid, he would recite the Takbeerat aloud."
"477","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that on the day of Eid al-Fitr, he would go towards the Eid ground in the morning when the sun had risen. He would recite the takbeerat in the Eid ground until the imam sat down, at which point he would stop reciting the takbeerat."
"478","Abu Huwaireth reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote a letter to Amr bin Hazm (may Allah be pleased with him) when he was at Najran, saying: ""Offer the Eid al-Adha prayer early and the Eid al-Fitr prayer with some delay, and also admonish and advise the people."""
"479","Safwan bin Salim narrates that the Prophet ﷺ used to eat something before going out to the Eidgah on the day of Eid al-Fitr, and he would also instruct others to do so."
"480","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he states: The Prophet (ﷺ) offered the Eid prayer in the Eidgah on the days of Eid; he did not offer any prayer before it nor after it. Then he came to the women and delivered a sermon to them while standing and instructed them to give charity. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The women gave their earrings and other items as charity."
"481","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that on the morning of Eid, he went to the Eid ground with the Prophet (ﷺ), then returned home and did not perform any prayer after nor before."
"482","It is narrated from Abdul Malik bin Ka'b (may Allah have mercy on him) that Ka'b bin Ujrah (may Allah be pleased with him) did not perform any prayer before or after the Eid prayer."
"483","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he states that during the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), we would not perform any prayer in the mosque on the days of Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha (after the Fajr prayer) until we arrived at the Eid ground, and when we returned from the Eid ground, we would pass by the mosque and perform prayer in it."
"484","It is narrated from Nafi' (may Allah have mercy on him) that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) would not perform any prayer on the day of Eid al-Fitr before the Eid prayer nor after it."
"485","Ja'far bin Muhammad (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that the Prophet (ﷺ), Abu Bakr, and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) said seven and five takbeers in the Eid and Istisqa prayers, and performed the prayer before the sermon, and recited aloud in them."
"486","It is narrated from Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that he pronounced seven and five takbeers in the Eid and Istisqa prayers and recited aloud."
"487","It is narrated from Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him) that Abu Ayyub Ansari and Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with them both) instructed Marwan to say seven takbirs in the first rak'ah and five takbirs in the second rak'ah of the Eid prayers."
"488","It is narrated from Nafi’, the freed slave of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: I attended the Eid al-Adha and Eid al-Fitr prayers with Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said seven takbirs before the recitation in the first rak’ah and five takbirs before the recitation in the second rak’ah."
"489","It is narrated from Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who states that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to perform the Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha prayers before the sermon."
"490","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the Eid prayer before the sermon. Then he addressed the people with a sermon. He thought that perhaps the women had not heard the voice, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went to them, preached and advised them, and instructed them to give charity. Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) was with him, holding out his garment in this manner (i.e., saying, ""Put in it""), so the women gave their earrings and other items (such as rings, etc.) in charity."
"491","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (ﷺ), Abu Bakr, and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) used to perform the Eid prayers before the sermon."
"492","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he reports from the Prophet (peace be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman (may Allah be pleased with them), as in the previous hadith."
"493","It is narrated from Ibn Sirin (may Allah have mercy on him) that after finishing the Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha prayers, the Prophet ﷺ would deliver the sermon while mounted on his camel."
"494","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Yazid Khatmi (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman (may Allah be pleased with them) used to perform the Eid prayer before the sermon, until the era of Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) came, and Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered the sermon first."
"495","It is narrated from Iyad bin Abdullah bin Sa’d bin Abi Sarh ﷺ that Abu Sa’id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “Marwan sent a man to me and to another man, whose name he mentioned. Marwan came with us to the Eid ground, and he began to ascend the pulpit, so I pulled him back. He said: O Abu Sa’id! What you know has been abandoned today. Abu Sa’id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I said three times in a loud voice, By Allah! You have brought an evil (way) in place of it.”"
"496","It is narrated from Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah (may Allah have mercy on him) that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) asked Abu Waqid Al-Laithi (may Allah be pleased with him): ""What would the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recite in the prayers of Eid al-Adha and Eid al-Fitr?"" He replied: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would recite: ﴿Qaf, and the Glorious Qur'an﴾ and ﴿The Hour has drawn near, and the moon has split﴾."""
"497","It is narrated from Ubaydullah bin Abdullah (may Allah have mercy on him) that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) asked Abu Waqid Al-Laithi (may Allah be pleased with him): ""What would the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recite in the prayers of Eid al-Adha and Eid al-Fitr?"" He replied: ""He (ﷺ) would recite: 'Qaf, by the Glorious Qur'an' (__QUR_N__) and 'The Hour has drawn near' (__QUR_N__).”"
"498","It is narrated from Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) delivered a sermon, he would stand leaning firmly on a spear."
"499","Ubaydullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah narrates that the Sunnah method is that the Imam delivers two sermons in the Eid prayers and separates them by sitting in between."
"500","It is narrated from Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) that during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, Friday and Eid coincided (on the same day. The Prophet ﷺ said to the people living in the elevated areas around Madinah: ""If anyone wishes to stay at home from either of these two without any excuse, he is permitted."""
"501","It is narrated from Abu Ubaid, the freed slave of Ibn Azhar, who says: I went to the Eid prayer ground with Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) to perform the Eid prayer. He led the prayer and then addressed the people, saying: ""Today, two Eids have come together for you, and whoever among the inhabitants of the surrounding settlements of Madinah wishes to wait for Jumu'ah may do so, and whoever wishes to return may go; I have given permission."""
"502","It is narrated from Abu Ubaid, the freed slave of Ibn Azhar, that I attended the Eid prayer with Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) while Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) was under siege."
"503","It is narrated from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the first ten days of Dhul-Hijjah begin and any one of you intends to offer a sacrifice, then he should not cut anything from his hair or skin (nails)."""
"504","It is narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sacrificed two speckled rams."
"505","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who states: We performed sacrifices with the Prophet (ﷺ) at the place of Hudaybiyyah; a camel was sacrificed on behalf of seven people, and a cow was also sacrificed on behalf of seven people."
"506","It is narrated from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) who states: We performed sacrifice at the place of Hudaybiyyah along with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him); the sacrifice of a camel was done on behalf of seven people, and the sacrifice of a cow was also done on behalf of seven people."
"507","It is narrated from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you should eat from his sacrificial meat after three days."""
"508","Abu Ubaid narrates from the freed slave of Ibn Azhar, who states: I was present with Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) on the occasion of Eid, and I heard him say: None of you should eat from the meat of his sacrifice after three days."
"509","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Waqid bin Abdullah that he reports: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating the meat of sacrifice after three days. Abdullah bin Abi Bakr says: I mentioned this to Amrah, and she said: Abdullah bin Waqid has spoken the truth. I heard Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) say: ""During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, some people from among the Bedouins came (to Medina) at the time of sacrifice, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Store it for three days and give the rest in charity."" Aisha further narrates: After that, it was said, O Messenger of Allah, people used to benefit from their sacrifices, collect its fat, and make water skins from it. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""So what happened now?"" or he said something similar. The companions said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, you forbade eating the meat of sacrifice after three days. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""I forbade you from eating the meat of sacrifice because some people had come from outside at the time of sacrifice. Now eat, store, and also give in charity."""
"510","It is narrated from Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade eating the meat of sacrifice after three days, then later said: ""Eat, take provisions, and store it."""
"511","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: With Allah’s help, we would slaughter as many animals as we could, and then take the remainder to Basra."
"512","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Zaid Al-Mazani (may Allah be pleased with him) that he stated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went out to the Eid ground to perform the prayer for seeking rain. He faced the Qiblah, turned his cloak inside out, and offered two units of prayer."
"513","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) offered two rak'ahs of Salat al-Istisqa in the Eid ground."
"514","Abdullah bin Zaid Al-Mazni (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went towards the Eid ground for the prayer of Istisqa. When he faced the Qiblah, he turned his cloak inside out."
"515","It is narrated from ‘Abbad bin Tamim (may Allah be pleased with him) that he states: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) offered the prayer of Istisqa (prayer for rain), and he was wearing a heavy black cloak. He grasped it from below and tried to turn it upwards, and when it became burdensome, he simply turned it over on his shoulders."
"516","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she states that during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, people were afflicted with severe famine. A Jew passed by them and said: ""If your companion (Muhammad ﷺ) wishes, as much rain as you want can be sent down upon you, but he does not like that rain should fall upon you."" The Prophet ﷺ was informed of the Jew's statement, so he said: ""Did he say this?"" The companions said: ""Yes."" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""I will seek help for the people of Najd in this famine, and I see that clouds are coming out from Aden, which I dislike. On such-and-such day, I promise you, I will supplicate for rain for you."" He said: When that day came, the people gathered early in the morning, and they had not yet dispersed when it began to rain, and then it continued to rain for a whole week."
"517","It is narrated from Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said, ""The livestock have perished and the roads are blocked, so pray to Allah (for rain)."" Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: It rained continuously from one Friday to the next. Then the same man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! The houses have collapsed, the roads have been cut off, and the livestock have been destroyed (due to the abundance of water)."" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood up and prayed: ""O Allah! Let the rain fall on the tops of the mountains, on the hills, in the valleys, and in the gardens."" (As a result of the supplication) the clouds parted from Madinah as if a cloth had been torn into pieces."
"518","It is narrated from Matlub bin Hantab that when rain would descend, the Prophet ﷺ would supplicate: ""O Allah, (send) rain of mercy, not of punishment, nor of trial, nor rain that destroys homes, nor rain that drowns. O Allah, (send rain) on the mountains and in the gardens. O Allah, send rain around us, not upon us."""
"519","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that whenever the Prophet ﷺ saw clouds in the sky, he would leave all work, face the Qiblah, and supplicate: ""O Allah! I seek refuge with You from the evil of what is in it."" If the clouds dispersed, he would praise Allah, and if it rained, he would say: ""O Allah, make this rain beneficial."""
"520","It is narrated from Matlub bin Hantab that when there was lightning or thunder in the sky, its effects could be seen on the face of the Prophet ﷺ, and when the rain would fall, the effects (of fear) would disappear."
"521","It is narrated from Urwah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: When any of you sees lightning or rain, he should not point towards it, rather he should abundantly mention its attributes."
"522","It is narrated from Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led us in the morning prayer at Hudaybiyyah after a night in which it had rained. When he finished the prayer, he turned to the people and said: ""Do you know what your Lord has said?"" The people replied: Allah and His Messenger know best. He (ﷺ) said: (Allah has said) 'This morning some of My servants have become believers in Me and some have become disbelievers. As for the one who said: We have been given rain by the grace and mercy of Allah, he is a believer in Me and a disbeliever in the stars. And as for the one who said: We have been given rain by such-and-such star, he is a disbeliever in Me and a believer in the stars.'"""
"523","Abdullah bin Abi Bakr narrates from his father: One night it rained upon the people. When the Prophet ﷺ came in the morning, he said to them: ""Last night, rain fell everywhere upon the entire earth."""
"524","It is narrated from Matlub bin Hantab that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""In every moment of the night and day, rain descends from the sky. Allah directs this (rain) wherever He wills."""
"525","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Allah Almighty sends the winds, and they bring water from the sky. Then they pass through the clouds and become filled in such a way (with water) as a pregnant she-camel is filled with milk, then rain is sent down."
"526","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""It is near that such rain will fall in Medina that none of the roofs of its inhabitants' houses will remain, and only the shade of hair will cover them."""
"527","Safwan bin Salim narrates that the Prophet ﷺ said: A rain will fall upon the people of Madinah such that there will not remain a single mud roof of any house of its inhabitants."
"528","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him), he states: It is near that rain will fall continuously in Madinah for forty nights, so that none of the mud roofs of the people of Madinah will remain intact."
"529","It is narrated from Salih bin Abdullah bin Zubair that Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him while he was building a dam of clay for water in Mecca: ""Make it hard and strong, for we find in the books that in the last era, floods will become great."""
"530","Saeed bin Musayyib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from his father, who narrated from his grandfather, that once a flood came in Makkah which filled the space between the two mountains (with water)."
"531","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Drought is not that rain does not fall upon you, but drought is that abundant rain falls upon you and the earth (due to being saline) produces nothing."""
"532","Yazid or Naufal bin Abdullah Al-Hashimi narrates that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""I have been made to stay on land with little rainfall, and it is between two springs of the sky: between the spring of 'Sham' and the spring of 'Ayn'."""
"533","It is narrated from Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that he stated: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Medina is between two springs of the sky, one is the spring of Syria and the other is the spring of Yemen, and this is a land with little rainfall."""
"534","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Amr that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""I have been helped by my eastern wind, and this wind used to bring punishment for the people before."""
"535","Safwan bin Salim narrates that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Do not curse or speak ill of the wind, and seek Allah's protection from the evil that is in it."""
"536","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: On the way to Makkah, people were overtaken by wind, and Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was going for Hajj. The wind became strong, so Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked those around him: Has any command regarding the wind reached you (from the Prophet ﷺ)? The people did not give any answer. Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I came to know about what Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) had asked regarding the wind. I hurried my camel until I reached Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), even though I was at the end of the people. I said: O Commander of the Faithful! I have learned that you inquired about the wind. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ""The wind is by the command of Allah; it brings both mercy and punishment. Do not speak ill of it. Ask Allah for the good that is in it, and seek refuge with Allah from the evil that is in it."""
"537","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Whenever a strong wind blew, the Prophet (ﷺ) would sit on his knees and recite: ""O Allah! Make it a mercy, not a punishment. O Allah! Make it a means of comfort, not a calamity."" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: It is in the Book of Allah: And We sent upon them a violent, raging wind. (__QUR_54_19__) And We sent upon them a barren wind. (__QUR_51_41__) And We send the laden winds. (__QUR_15_22__) And He sends the winds as glad tidings. (__QUR_30_46__)"
